==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|treat with kid gloves}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|kid glove}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-handle with kid gloves.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*|head=[[handle]] [[with]] [[kid glove]]s}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To treat something very [[delicately]] or [[carefully]].
#: {{ux|en|The campaign staff cautioned the candidate to '''handle''' the issue '''with kid gloves'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Treasury of David: {{nb...|Containing an Original Exposition of the Book of Psalms; A Collection of Illustrative Extracts From the Whole Range of literature; A Series of Homiletical hints Upon Almost Every Verse; And Lists of Writers Upon Each Psalm}}|author=[[w:Charles Spurgeon|C. H. Spurgeon]]|volume=VI|location=London|publisher=Passmore and Alabaster, 4 paternoster Buildings|year=1884|chapter=Psalm One Hundred and Nineteen—Verses 113 to 120, Exposition|page=260|pageurl=https://www.google.com/books/edition/Psalm_CXIX_to_CXXIV/q9Q0461zG6gC?hl=en&gbpv=1&pg=PA260&printsec=frontcover|passage=He does not trifle with them, or''' handle them with kid gloves'''. No, he judges them to be the scum of the earth, and he treats them accordingly by putting them away.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=http://www.theguardian.com/politics/2003/aug/03/israelandthepalestinians.pressandpublishing|author=Stephen Pritchard|title=Racist or just anti-Sharon?|date=2003-08-03|work=The Guardian|passage=[Richard] Ingrams has always enjoyed a reputation for insensitivity. As with other columnists in the British press, he treads on toes to make his point and rides roughshod over issues that others '''handle with kid gloves''', or avoid altogether.}}

